            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes. You can set [`current_dir` argument to `true` in `sections.recent.files()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9968f6e221ae7bdac57a910c5bf2026186aa023c/doc/mini-starter.txt#L367-L368). This requires building your own items. [Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9968f6e221ae7bdac57a910c5bf2026186aa023c/doc/mini-starter.txt#L88-L103) is an example.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes. You can set <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9968f6e221ae7bdac57a910c5bf2026186aa023c/doc/mini-starter.txt#L367-L368\"><code class=\"notranslate\">current_dir</code> argument to <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">sections.recent.files()</code></a>. This requires building your own items. <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9968f6e221ae7bdac57a910c5bf2026186aa023c/doc/mini-starter.txt#L88-L103\">Here</a> is an example.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yes. You can set current_dir argument to true in sections.recent.files(). This requires building your own items. Here is an example.",
